{"id":"word:hebrew:H3988","type":"word","title":"מָאַס","subtitle":"H3988 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"to spurn ; also (intransitively) to disappear","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מָאַס (H3988) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: v.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 76 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מָאַס (mâʼaç) means to spurn ; also (intransitively) to disappear First listed occurrence: 1Sam 8 7."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מָאַס","transliteration":"mâʼaç","pronunciation":"maw-as'","strong":"H3988","lemmaId":"hebrew:H3988","partOfSpeech":"v","forms":["מָאָ֔סוּ","מָאָ֗סוּ","מָאַ֗סְתָּ","מָאַ֣ס","אֶמְאַ֗ס"],"morphs":[["HVqp3cp",12],["HVqp2ms",6],["HVqp3ms",5],["HVqi1cs",5],["HVqp2mp",3],["HC/Vqw3mp",3],["HC/Vqw3ms",3],["HVqp1cs",3],["HVqa",3],["HVqi3ms",3]]},"definitions":{"short":"to spurn ; also (intransitively) to disappear","usage":"abhor, cast away (off), contemn, despise, disdain, (become) loathe(some), melt away, refuse, reject, reprobate, × utterly, vile person.","full":"H3988. ma 'ac I. [ מָאַס ] verb reject (Late Hebrew id .; Aramaic מְאַס reject, despise ; Ba ES 15 compare (dubious) Arabic lightly esteem (Kam.); Assyrian ma°âsu is perhaps destroy Meissn Suppl. 55 ); — Qal Perfect 3masculine singular מָאַס Isa 8:6 4 t; suffix מְאָסָם Psa 53:6 ; 2 masculine singular מָאַסְתָּ Jer 14:19 3 t.; מָאַסְתָּה Judg 9:38 ; 1Sam 15:26 22 t. Perfect; Imperfect יִמְאַס Job 8:20 3 t; יִמְאָ֑ס Psa 36:5 ; Job 36:5 ; suffix וַיִּמְאָֽסְךָ 1Sam 15:23 , 26 ; for וְאֶמְאָֽסְאךָ Hosea 4:6 (so Baer, compare De Complut. Var. 18 f. ; not ׳וָא van d. H) read וְאֶמְאסְךָ ; 3 masculine plural יִמְאֲסוּ Jer 6:19 2 t.; יִמְאָס֑וּן Isa 31:7 ; 12t. Imperfect; Infinitive absolute מָאוֺס 7:15-16 , מָאֹס Jer 14:19 ; Lam 5:22 ; cstr . מָֽאָסְכֶם Isa 30:12 ; מָאֳסָם Amos 2:4 ; Participle מוֺאֵס Prov 15:32 ; מֹאֵס Isa 33:15 , feminine מֹאֶסֶת Ezek 21:15 (